{
  "dom_id": "step-621978",
  "name": "Solving Problems Using Division of Rational Numbers",
  "problem": "Sometimes we know the total change in a quantity and want to find how much the quantity changes during each equal time period.\n\nIn these situations, we use division.\n\nFor example, suppose a total of $\\[math]24$ is withdrawn from a bank account over $6$ days in equal amounts.\n\nSince money is withdrawn, the total change in the balance is $-\\[/math]24$.\n\nTo find the change each day, we divide the total change by the number of days:\n\n$$\n-24 \\div 6\n$$\n\nEvaluating the quotient, we get\n\n$$\n-24 \\div 6 = -4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the balance changes by $-\\[math]4$ each day.",
